Native Amiga standard-packet placement regression

Build with test-dos-packetplacement or test-dos-packetplacement-quick.
The native Amiga DOS component normal/quick targets select this test.
Run on a quiet stock 2 MiB Chip-only machine, one instance at a time.

The test reserves a small arena and all remaining packet-sized free blocks
while Forbid is held, then releases two separated holes in the arena.
AllocDosObject(DOS_STDPKT) must use ordinary allocation direction, selecting
the lower suitable hole, and initialize its public message/packet link.
The test restores all reserved memory before printing its results.

This exercises actual DOS/Exec allocation, not patched allocation vectors.
Forced MEMF_REVERSE fails one of five checks; ordinary placement passes all
five. AllocVec metadata and alignment are included when reserving other holes.
The companion Hunk-placement test covers explicit reverse Hunk requests.
